-- l4 batch over a record declared under a section heading and decoded by the
-- rules twice, once with the type written behind its heading and once bare
-- (the sections nest: `Settings` resolves to the `Pricing` one from `Use`).
-- A decode names the record as it is DECLARED, behind its heading, whichever way
-- the decode site spelled the type, so the two decodes are one entry, and it
-- is the entry the WITH default of the same record carries (assumed, not ruled:
-- the review of the combined branch, 2026-10-12, following overnight card O6).

§ `Pricing`

DECLARE Settings HAS
  limit IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY 10

§ `Use`

GIVEN s IS A STRING
GIVETH AN EITHER STRING `Pricing`.Settings
parseQ s MEANS JSONDECODE s

GIVEN s IS A STRING
GIVETH AN EITHER STRING Settings
parseB s MEANS JSONDECODE s

GIVETH A NUMBER
lq MEANS CONSIDER parseQ "{}"
    WHEN RIGHT st THEN st's limit
    WHEN LEFT e THEN 0

GIVETH A NUMBER
lb MEANS CONSIDER parseB "{}"
    WHEN RIGHT st THEN st's limit
    WHEN LEFT e THEN 0

@export default go
GIVEN amount IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE go amount IS lq PLUS lb PLUS (Settings WITHAL)'s limit PLUS (`Pricing`.Settings WITHAL)'s limit
